// Title: PDF File Created By RegEdit.EXE
// Sigma ID: 145095eb-e273-443b-83d0-f9b519b7867b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-07-08 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects the creation of a file with the ".pdf" extension by the "RegEdit.exe" process. This
//   indicates that a user is trying to print/save a registry key as a PDF in order to potentially
//   extract sensitive information and bypass defenses.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://sensepost.com/blog/2024/dumping-lsa-secrets-a-story-about-task-decorrelation/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_regedit_print_as_pdf.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\regedit.exe" and FolderPath endswith ".pdf"
